Burnoff

Client-side Sentinel-2 SWIR flare detection with peer-to-peer sync.

  Browser                              Browser (peer)
 +---------------------+              +---------------------+
 |  Map + UI           |   WebRTC /   |  Map + UI           |
 |  LWW-Map CRDT <------+-- WS sync ->+---> LWW-Map CRDT   |
 |  +---------------+  |              |  +---------------+  |
 |  | detect        |  |              |  | detect        |  |
 |  +-------+-------+  |              |  +-------+-------+  |
 +---------+|-----------+              +---------+|-----------+
            | HTTP range requests                |
            v                                    v
      Element84 STAC -- Sentinel-2 L2A COGs

Open the map, navigate to an area of interest, select date quarters,
click Detect. The app downloads Sentinel-2 imagery and runs the
detection algorithm entirely in your browser. Results sync between
all open sessions via WebRTC -- when you detect, idle peers
automatically split the work.


Quick Start

  make serve     # Dev server on :8000 + signaling on :4444


How It Works

Gas flares emit strongly in shortwave infrared. Burnoff reads
cloud-optimised GeoTIFF bands (B12, B11, B8A) from Element84's STAC
catalogue via windowed HTTP range requests, runs a multi-stage
detection pipeline client-side in a Web Worker, and clusters
detections across dates using anchor-based spatial merging.

Detection pipeline (per 256x256 pixel block):
  1. Cloud screening via SCL band
  2. DN to surface reflectance, background median for contrast threshold
  3. Fused brightness + contrast + thermal filter pass
  4. Connected components, cluster quality filters, warm-region halo rejection
  5. Cross-date clustering (grid-indexed, anchor-based merge within 50m)

P2P sync: results are stored in a custom LWW-Map CRDT, persisted
locally via IndexedDB, and synced across peers via WebRTC
DataChannels with a custom binary sync protocol.


Project Structure

  web/
    app.js              Map viewer, CRDT sync, cross-date clustering
    detect.js           Detection algorithm (Web Worker)
    crdt.js             LWW-Map CRDT with binary codec
    sync.js             Sync protocol, awareness, validation
    rtc.js              WebRTC DataChannel mesh
    store.js            IndexedDB persistence with batched flushes
    utm.js              UTM <-> WGS84 projection (hand-rolled Transverse Mercator)
    index.html          Entry point
    style.css           UI styles
  signal/
    server.js           WebSocket signaling relay (RFC 6455, zero dependencies)
    Dockerfile          Cloud Run container for production signaling
  test/                 Determinism + P2P tests

Zero npm dependencies. MapLibre GL and geotiff.js are loaded from
CDN. Everything else -- CRDT, WebRTC mesh, sync protocol, IndexedDB
persistence, UTM projection, and signaling -- uses browser and
Node.js builtins only.


References

Faruolo et al. (2024) The DAFI v2 algorithm for gas flare detection
https://doi.org/10.1088/1748-9326/ad82fb
